# =============================================================================
# RetroPick monorepo — local env template (host-run API / indexer)
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root if tooling expects it, or export vars in shell.
# Do not commit `.env` or `.env.local` (see root `.gitignore`).
#
# Docker Compose sets equivalent values in `docker-compose.yml` — use that for
# the full stack (Postgres + API + indexer + ops).
#
# Docker Compose interpolates RETROPICK_COMPOSE_DATABASE_URL (default postgres:5432 in docker-compose.yml).
# Docker Desktop bridge issues: compose.desktop-hairpin.env or pnpm docker:up:desktop — see README.
#
# Contract / Foundry tooling: see `package/contract/.env.example`.
# Operator UI (Next): see `apps/ops/.env.local.example`.
# =============================================================================

# --- Go API (`go run ./cmd/api` from `apps/backend`) ---
# Required. From the host, Compose publishes Postgres on 5433 (see docker-compose.yml).
# Use 5432 only if you run Postgres directly on the machine (no port remap).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://retropick:retropick@127.0.0.1:5433/retropick?sslmode=disable

# JSON-RPC for Base Sepolia (default in code if unset).
RPC_URL=https://sepolia.base.org

# HTTP listen port (default 8080).
PORT=8080

# Watchlist mutations: default requires EIP-191 signature + nonce. Set 0 for unsigned POSTs (Compose sets 0 for local UX;
# never expose unsigned mode on a public API — any caller could mutate any wallet’s watchlist).
# RETROPICK_WATCHLIST_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE=0

# Optional tuning (see `apps/backend/internal/config/config.go`).
# DB_MAX_CONNS=16
# DB_MIN_CONNS=2
# DB_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL=30s
# LIVE_RPC_TIMEOUT=15s
# LIVE_RPC_GLOBAL_CACHE_TTL=5s
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Gasless testnet faucet relay (`POST /api/v1/user/faucet-relay`) — Base Sepolia only.
# Fund the relayer EOA with Base Sepolia ETH. Never commit the private key.
# FAUCET_RELAY_ENABLED=1
# FAUCET_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...
# Optional: max EIP-712 deadline skew from now (Go duration, default 15m).
# FAUCET_RELAY_DEADLINE_MAX=15m

# --- Indexer (`go run ./cmd/indexer`) ---
# Uses the same DATABASE_URL and RPC_URL as the API.
# INDEXER_LOOKBACK_BLOCKS=50000

# --- Production API (Vercel Go or external host) ---
# Use managed Postgres; providers often require TLS on the connection string.
# Supabase serverless/Vercel commonly uses the transaction pooler (`:6543`):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Migrations from local/CI can use direct connection (`:5432`) when needed:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Browser apps on another origin (e.g. Vercel) must be allowed explicitly when CORS_STRICT=1:
# CORS_STRICT=1
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com,https://your-project.vercel.app
# Optional for all Vercel preview deployments:
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_PATTERNS=https://*.vercel.app


  vercel env add DATABASE_URL production
  # paste:
  #
  postgresql://postgres.udhtksxrhjywyqqtxrnw:YOUR_DB_PASSWORD@aws-1-ap-southeast-2.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require

  vercel env add RPC_URL production
  # paste:
  # https://sepolia.base.org

  vercel env add CORS_STRICT production
  # paste:
  # 1

  vercel env add CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS production
  # paste:
  # https://YOUR_FE_DOMAIN.vercel.app

  vercel env add CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_PATTERNS production
  # paste:
  # https://*.vercel.app

Nice, backend env vars are in place now.

  Do these next steps in order:

  1. Go back to backend folder and redeploy so new env vars apply:

  cd ~/dev/Project/RetroPick/monorepo-base/apps/backend
  vercel --prod

  2. Test backend:

  curl -sS https://backend-retropick-base.vercel.app/api/v1/health
  curl -sS https://backend-retropick-base.vercel.app/api/v1/markets

  3. If those work, wire frontend to this backend:

  cd ~/dev/Project/RetroPick/monorepo-base/apps/fe-v1
  vercel link
  vercel env rm NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL production
  vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL production
  # value: https://backend-retropick-base.vercel.app
  vercel --prod

  4. Open frontend URL and confirm market loading no longer calls
     127.0.0.1:8080.

  If curl returns an error, paste the exact output and I’ll diagnose
  immediately.
